    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Moses Peltier opened a general store and blacksmith in 1886, sparking the town’s first post office the next year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fruitland_washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Long before Europeans arrived, the Colville, Lake, and Spokane tribes had lived here for thousands of years.",
